{"name":"Thicket","hex":"#69865b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"thicket","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dense, but generally small, growth of shrubs, bushes or small trees; a copse.","A dense aggregation of other things, concrete or abstract."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thicket"}],"entries":[{"title":"Thicket","blocks":[{"text":"A thicket is a very dense stand of trees or tall shrubs, often dominated by only one or a few species to the exclusion of all others. They may be formed by species that shed large numbers of highly viable seeds that are able to germinate in the shelter of the maternal plants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Betula_pendula_%28fall_colors%29_2.jpg/330px-Betula_pendula_%28fall_colors%29_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thicket"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"thicket":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c9/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-thicket.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c9/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-thicket.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-thicket.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/c9/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-thicket.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-thicket.wav.ogg"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/02/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-thicket.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/02/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-thicket.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-thicket.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/